<article class="env-definition" id="01HT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01HT">Definition <span data-tag="01HT">26.5.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>standard open covering</em> of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a covering $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) = \bigcup _{i = 1}^ n D(f_ i)$, where $f_1, \ldots , f_ n \in R$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Suppose that $D(f) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a standard open. A <em>standard open covering</em> of $D(f)$ is a covering $D(f) = \bigcup _{i = 1}^ n D(g_ i)$, where $g_1, \ldots , g_ n \in R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>